          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            The notion of
            %em elliptic chain complex
            is the generalization of the notion of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/elliptic+operator"} elliptic operator
            from single
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/linear+maps"} linear maps
            to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/chain+complexes"} chain complexes
            of linear maps.
          %h2#definition Definition
          %p
            For
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+manifold"} smooth manifold
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %msub
                    %mi E
                    %mi k
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %mrow
                      %mi k
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi ℤ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{E_k\}_{k \in \mathbb{Z}}
            a collection of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vector+bundles"} vector bundles
            over
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/chain+complex"} chain complex
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+operators"} differential operators
            between the spaces of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sections"} sections
            of these bundles
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ⋯
                  %mo →
                  %mi Γ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi E
                    %mrow
                      %mi k
                      %mo +
                      %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi P
                        %mi k
                  %mi Γ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi E
                    %mi k
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %mi ⋯
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\cdots \to \Gamma(E_{k+1}) \stackrel{P_k}{\to} \Gamma(E_k) \to \cdots
          %p
            is called an
            %strong elliptic chain complex
            if the corresponding sequence of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symbol+of+a+differential+operator"} symbols
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ⋯
                  %mo →
                  %msup
                    %mi π
                    %mo *
                  %msub
                    %mi E
                    %mrow
                      %mi k
                      %mo +
                      %mn 1
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mrow
                      %mi σ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi P
                        %mi k
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %msup
                    %mi π
                    %mo *
                  %msub
                    %mi E
                    %mi k
                  %mo →
                  %mi ⋯
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\cdots \to \pi^* E_{k+1} \stackrel{\sigma(P_k)}{\to} \pi^* E_k \to \cdots
          %p
            (where
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi π
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %msup
                    %mi T
                    %mo *
                  %mi X
                  %mo →
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi \colon T^* X \to X
            is the
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cotangent+bundle"} cotangent bundle
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/exact+sequence"} exact sequence
          %p
            For instance (
            %a{:href => "#Pati"}> Pati, def. 9.4.1
            ).
          %p
            For a single differential operator
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi P
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P
            this says that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mn 0
                  %mo →
                  %msup
                    %mi π
                    %mo *
                  %msub
                    %mi E
                    %mn 1
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mrow
                      %mi σ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi P
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %msup
                    %mi π
                    %mo *
                  %msub
                    %mi E
                    %mn 0
                  %mo →
                  %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 0 \to \pi^* E_1 \stackrel{\sigma(P)}{\to} \pi^* E_0 \to 0
            is exact, which means that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi σ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi P
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sigma(P)
            is an
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism"} isomorphism
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi P
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P
            is an
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/elliptic+operator"} elliptic operator
          %h2#properties Properties
          %h3#AtiyahBottLemma Atiyah-Bott lemma
          %p
            If
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi ℰ
                  %mo ,
                  %mi d
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\mathcal{E}, d)
            is an elliptic complex of smooth
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sections"} sections
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℰ
                  %mo =
                  %msub
                    %mi Γ
                    %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi E
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{E} = \Gamma_X(E)
            of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vector+bundle"} vector bundle
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi E
                  %mo →
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E \to X
            overa
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact+topological+space"} compact
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/closed+manifold"} closed manifold
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi ℰ
                  %mo ,
                  %mi d
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ↪
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mover
                    %mi ℰ
                    %mo ¯
                  %mo ,
                  %mi d
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  (\mathcal{E},d) \hookrightarrow (\overline{\mathcal{E}}, d)
          %p
            into the complex of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/distribution"} distributional
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sections"} sections
            is a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quasi-isomorphism"} quasi-isomorphism
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+equivalence"} homotopy equivalence
          %p
            This is due to (
            %a{:href => "#AtiyahBott"}> Atiyah-Bott
            ). A localized refinement (suitable for
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/factorization+algebras+of+local+observables"} factorization algebras of local observables
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#Gwilliam"} Gwilliam, lemma 5.2.13
          %h2#examples Examples
          %p
            The classical examples of elliptic complexes are discussed also in (
            %a{:href => "#Gilkey"}> Gilkey section 3
            ).
          %h3#de_rham_complex de Rham complex
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            be a compact smooth manifold. Then the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/de+Rham+complex"} de Rham complex
            is an elliptic complex. The corresponding
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/index+of+an+elliptic+complex"} index of an elliptic complex
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Euler+characteristic"} Euler characteristic
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Ind
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi Ω
                    %mo •
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ,
                  %mi d
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mi χ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %munderover
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                    %mrow
                      %mi p
                      %mo =
                      %mn 0
                    %mrow
                      %mi dim
                      %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mn 1
                  %msup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi p
                  %mi dim
                  %msubsup
                    %mi H
                    %mi dR
                    %mi p
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mi ℂ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  Ind(\Omega^\bullet(X),d)
                  \=
                  \\chi(X)
                  \=
                  \\sum_{p = 0}^{dim X} (-1)^p  dim H_{dR}^p(X, \mathbb{C})
          %h3#the_yangmills_complex The Yang-Mills complex
          %p (…)
          %h3#the_dolbeault_complex The Dolbeault complex
          %p
            (…)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dolbeault+complex"} Dolbeault complex
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/index+of+an+elliptic+complex"} index of an elliptic complex
            of the Dolbeault complex is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/arithmetic+genus"} arithmetic genus
          %h3#spin_complex Spin complex
          %p
            (…) index is
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/A-hat+genus"} A-hat genus
            (…)
